. "$HOME/.cargo/env"

# Secrets for EVERY zsh, not just interactive ones.
#
# `.zshrc` also sources this, but `.zshrc` is read only by interactive shells —
# so anything driving zsh non-interactively (Claude Code's Bash tool, `zsh -c`,
# `ssh host '<cmd>'`, a script with a zsh shebang) came up without GH_TOKEN and
# `gh` reported itself logged out. That looks exactly like a token that was
# never set up, which is the wrong conclusion and has cost time twice.
#
# `.zshenv` is the one file zsh reads on every invocation, so it is the only
# place that fixes the non-interactive case. Same shape as the workstation fix
# that moved the `.secrets` source above `.bashrc`'s interactive guard.
#
# Keep everything above and inside this guard SILENT: stray output on a
# non-interactive shell breaks scp/rsync/sftp. `~/.secrets` is only `export`
# lines and a `case`, so it qualifies — check again before adding anything to it.
[ -f "$HOME/.secrets" ] && source "$HOME/.secrets"
